      "title": "Hegseth fires top military planner even as Trump plans fresh Iran strikes",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/hegseth-fires-top-military-planner-even-as-trump-plans-fresh-iran-strikes-126102900113_1.html",
      "description": "Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth has fired the Pentagon's top military planner, a defence official said Wednesday, the latest in a series of generals to be ousted and one that comes even as President Donald Trump is weighing renewed strikes on Iran in the eight-month-long war.\nArmy Lt Gen Brett Sylvia was removed as head of strategy, plans and policy on the Joint Chiefs of Staff. He is the second general to be ousted from the post, known in military circles as the \"J5\", under Hegseth. His predecessor, Lt Gen Joseph McGee, was forced to retire last October.\nThe defence official, who spoke on condition of anonymity to discuss sensitive personnel matters, said there is no immediate replacement for Sylvia and no reason has been given for the firing. The move was reported earlier by The Atlantic.\nA spokesperson for the Joint Staff said \"the Chairman, the Joint Staff, and the Joint Force extend our deepest gratitude to Lt Gen Brett Sylvia and his family for their 32 years of distinguished .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-29T04:35:17"
    },
